{"base_rate":0.32808398950131235,"brier":0.1426245406824147,"bss":0.35301497031249995,"bss_hi":0.4327648438816784,"bss_lo":0.27144731200086414,"chart":{"base":[487.4,57.9],"fp":[248.1,312.2],"lead":"62,210.2 272,160.4 482,121.1 692,49.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.35 — higher than 66% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +13pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 14% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 89% → rained 71%"},"rel":"64.3,455.9 126.9,377.4 337.7,181.7 620.4,158.2"},"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10841207349081361,"ess":499.8755954811485,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Washington</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Washington rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>73%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nWASHINGTON 2.2 ESE, 5.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.35, ranked 72 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(43&ndash;115) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>214</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Washington</b> <span class=\"muted\">United States</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.35</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>43&ndash;115\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Washington &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Washington\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 62.59357142857143,369.0 77.293,341.05 112.54394736842104,295.7894736842105 173.83417721518987,225.34177215189874 253.5384210526316,137.73684210526318 337.6128,61.68000000000001 404.556923076923,18.0 404.556923076923,36.666666666666686 337.6128,129.62666666666667 253.5384210526316,219.1578947368421 173.83417721518987,299.0632911392405 112.54394736842104,353.2631578947368 77.293,377.45 62.59357142857143,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"262.5774278215223\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"262.5774278215223\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,376.89719626168227 62.59357142857143,364.6666666666667 77.293,359.25 112.54394736842104,252.68421052631578 173.83417721518987,170.0506329113924 253.5384210526316,113.78947368421052 337.6128,129.62666666666667 404.556923076923,116.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 214 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"376.89719626168227\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"62.59357142857143\" cy=\"364.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"77.293\" cy=\"359.25\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"112.54394736842104\" cy=\"252.68421052631578\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 33%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"173.83417721518987\" cy=\"170.0506329113924\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"253.5384210526316\" cy=\"113.78947368421052\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 79%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"337.6128\" cy=\"129.62666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.556923076923\" cy=\"116.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(33%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Washington the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.46) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.12).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.124</td><td class='num'>11.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.389</td><td class='num'>8.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.432</td><td class='num'>8.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.462</td><td class='num'>7.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":38.89511,"lon":-77.03637,"n":762,"n_cities":213,"name":"Washington","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":214,"obs":0.014018691588785047,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.012976190476190474,"n":84,"obs":0.047619047619047616,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.05450000000000001,"n":80,"obs":0.0625,"sig":false},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.154078947368421,"n":76,"obs":0.35526315789473684,"sig":true},{"hi":0.44700000000000045,"lo":0.22,"mean":0.32721518987341774,"n":79,"obs":0.5822784810126582,"sig":true},{"hi":0.6680000000000007,"lo":0.44700000000000045,"mean":0.5523684210526316,"n":76,"obs":0.7368421052631579,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.6680000000000007,"mean":0.7898666666666667,"n":75,"obs":0.6933333333333334,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9789743589743588,"n":78,"obs":0.7307692307692307,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.2,"provisional":false,"rank":72,"rank_hi":115.04999999999995,"rank_lo":43.0,"reliability":0.0215932970504873,"resolution":0.09694394706242909,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"washington","station":"WASHINGTON 2.2 ESE","timezone":"America/New_York"}